WEBVTT

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:47.965
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.468
I must be crazy. I really must be.

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:54.638
I still had leave left, but I just had to come crawling back.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.098
Darn it.

00:00:56.682 --> 00:00:58.934
But still, it's good to have you in the mess hall.

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:00.852
It feels full and lively, sir.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:04.773
Right? I do have a pretty big presence, don't I?

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:09.736
You have advanced to Intermediate Cook.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.156
Your Basic Knife Skills speed has increased by 1.5 times.

00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:23.709
Was he always that fast with a knife?

00:01:35.304 --> 00:01:36.930
Oh, Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

00:01:37.014 --> 00:01:38.223
You can take a break. I'll be done in a flash.

00:01:38.307 --> 00:01:39.391
All right. Wait, what?

00:01:40.392 --> 00:01:41.602
Aren't you pushing yourself too hard?

00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:43.812
This is nothing.

00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:48.317
Oh, right. Could you toss me the sesame seeds?

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.401
Here!

00:01:49.568 --> 00:01:50.569
Yes, thank you.

00:01:56.867 --> 00:01:57.909
Impressive.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:15.052
Beef bulgogi, four stars. Stir-fried anchovies, four stars.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.221
Level up.

00:02:18.305 --> 00:02:19.306
AVAILABLE SKILLS

00:02:19.389 --> 00:02:22.684
New Skill available. Check Gourmet Rating.

00:02:22.851 --> 00:02:24.853
Gourmet Rating? What's that?

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.524
Fulfill the Gourmet Rating to earn additional rewards.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.860
So, are we ready for the guys to come in?

00:02:32.361 --> 00:02:34.780
GOURMET RATING

00:02:34.863 --> 00:02:36.448
This is so cool.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:40.952
GOURMET RATING

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:52.047
What, you punk? Are you laughing at your senior now?

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.091
No, sir.

00:02:55.384 --> 00:02:58.637
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun, what's your favorite dish?

00:02:58.804 --> 00:03:03.016
I don't eat for taste. I eat to see how much protein I'm getting.

00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:08.063
Oh, protein is very important, sir.

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:10.065
You don't sound very convinced.

00:03:10.148 --> 00:03:13.318
Hey, protein is essential for building muscle, you know.

00:03:13.443 --> 00:03:14.778
All right. Salute.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:18.990
GOURMET RATING

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:22.828
GOURMET RATING

00:03:25.163 --> 00:03:28.250
Kang Seong-jae, stop making the food so delicious, all right?

00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:31.294
- I keep gaining weight because of you. - Listen to you.

00:03:31.628 --> 00:03:34.297
You're talking like Kang Seong-jae did all the cooking.

00:03:34.923 --> 00:03:38.301
You can tell Kang Seong-jae made this just by how good it looks, sir.

00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:42.472
- You are acting up - Enjoy your meal, sir.

00:03:42.556 --> 00:03:43.724
Now that I'm powerless before my discharge, right?

00:03:43.807 --> 00:03:44.850
- Enjoy your meal, sir. - Thank you.

00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:46.852
- You don't even answer me. - Enjoy your meal.

00:03:46.935 --> 00:03:48.562
- Enjoy your meal. - Enjoy your meal.

00:03:48.645 --> 00:03:52.816
Today's menu is Korean Traditional Style One, Two, Three, Four, and Five.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:58.572
GOURMET RATING

00:04:03.785 --> 00:04:06.830
GOURMET RATING

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.957
You could've just said home-style Korean meal. Why make it sound so complicated?

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.500
Home-style Korean meal. Oh, so you understood?

00:04:10.876 --> 00:04:14.421
The very nature of a dish changes depending on the name it's given.

00:04:14.504 --> 00:04:15.505
Yes, sure.

00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:17.799
What would someone who only eats tofu and kimchi know about it?

00:04:17.883 --> 00:04:19.760
Jeez, you think I eat it because I want to?

00:04:19.843 --> 00:04:22.012
I'd eat better stuff if we had it. I eat it because there's nothing else.

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.352
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae, you got something to say?

00:04:30.353 --> 00:04:34.107
- No, sir. Enjoy your meal. - How silly.

00:04:38.361 --> 00:04:39.404
What a jerk.

00:04:47.162 --> 00:04:52.292
GOURMET RATING

00:04:53.627 --> 00:04:55.962
GOURMET RATING

00:04:56.046 --> 00:04:58.673
What are you staring at? Where's my soup?

00:04:58.757 --> 00:05:02.719
Private First Class Tak Mun-ik, I didn't realize you were so picky.

00:05:03.595 --> 00:05:04.930
Hey, TMI.

00:05:05.013 --> 00:05:06.848
Were you being sassy and complaining about the food?

00:05:06.932 --> 00:05:09.309
Would a worthless Private First Class like myself dare do such a thing, sir?

00:05:09.392 --> 00:05:10.977
I should just be grateful for whatever I'm served.

00:05:11.353 --> 00:05:12.437
Right.

00:05:20.445 --> 00:05:23.198
The stir-fried anchovies are well-cooked and not too sticky.

00:05:24.115 --> 00:05:27.911
The beef bulgogi isn't overdone, so it's still tender and juicy.

00:06:02.404 --> 00:06:03.822
And the seasoning is perfect, sir.

00:06:14.457 --> 00:06:18.003
You have fulfilled the Gourmet Rating for all the Ganglim Outpost Soldiers.

00:06:19.004 --> 00:06:21.047
You have earned bonus Experience Points.

00:06:21.131 --> 00:06:22.424
INTERMEDIATE COOK

00:06:26.011 --> 00:06:27.345
It's true that lately

00:06:28.138 --> 00:06:29.890
Even when I complete a Quest, my Experience Points

00:06:29.973 --> 00:06:31.433
Don't increase like they used to.

00:06:32.726 --> 00:06:34.644
The higher the grade of the dish you complete

00:06:34.728 --> 00:06:37.105
The more Experience Points you can acquire.

00:06:37.647 --> 00:06:39.232
Higher grade?

00:06:39.858 --> 00:06:45.155
Oh, now that I think about it I've never made a five-star dish before.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.702
EARN MORE EXPERIENCE POINTS BY COMPLETING HIGHER-GRADE DISHES

00:06:54.789 --> 00:06:57.334
EPISODE 9

00:07:21.566 --> 00:07:24.778
Frozen yellow croaker. Grade C from Jeju Island.

00:07:25.153 --> 00:07:26.404
Grade C?

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:32.160
Can I make a five-star dish with this?

00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:40.877
Whatever, let's just do it.

00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:56.977
FRIED YELLOW CROAKER: SPRINKLE A SMALL AMOUNT

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:58.186
OF SALT, COOKING WINE, AND LEMON JUICE

00:08:09.781 --> 00:08:12.909
Hero, the oil is hot enough.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:27.090
What are you up to again?

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:33.805
- Just finish it. - Yes, sir.

00:08:42.105 --> 00:08:45.316
TERRIFYING MINESWEEPER

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:46.401
RESPECTED BATTALION COMMANDER

00:08:51.489 --> 00:08:55.285
- Salute! Yes, Battalion Commander. - Seok-ho, have you had lunch?

00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:57.787
Yes, I have. Have you eaten, Battalion Commander?

00:08:57.871 --> 00:08:59.664
I always make sure to eat well.

00:08:59.873 --> 00:09:01.541
From the sound of your voice, Seok-ho, you sound

00:09:01.624 --> 00:09:03.918
Completely out of energy, as if you skipped lunch.

00:09:04.002 --> 00:09:05.295
Oh, that's not it.

00:09:06.087 --> 00:09:08.965
Come on, I can tell just by the sound of your voice.

00:09:09.215 --> 00:09:11.926
It's plain as day that you're sulking because Min-gu got promoted.

00:09:12.802 --> 00:09:15.221
Is that so? I'm really fine.

00:09:15.305 --> 00:09:18.183
Min-gu might have gotten a bit of a head start

00:09:18.266 --> 00:09:21.227
But no one knows who will reach the finish line first, you know?

00:09:21.895 --> 00:09:24.731
I'll make sure to back you up during the next promotion review

00:09:24.814 --> 00:09:25.815
So don't worry.

00:09:25.899 --> 00:09:28.818
Battalion Commander, your words alone are more than enough. Thank you.

00:09:30.361 --> 00:09:33.406
Anyway, to congratulate the guys getting promoted

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:35.867
The Regimental Commander wants everyone to gather at the Officers' Mess.

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:38.745
- The Company Commander has to be there. - Well, if you're inviting me

00:09:38.828 --> 00:09:40.163
I'll definitely be there.

00:09:40.455 --> 00:09:43.208
The Ganglim men went through a lot because of the typhoon.

00:09:43.291 --> 00:09:45.919
Bring the Outpost Commander and Private First Class Kang Seong-jae with you.

00:09:47.837 --> 00:09:50.465
But why Private First Class Kang Seong-jae?

00:09:51.216 --> 00:09:54.052
I just keep getting cravings for his cooking.

00:09:54.385 --> 00:09:56.471
And it seems the Regimental Commander is curious too.

00:09:58.723 --> 00:09:59.974
Battalion Commander.

00:10:00.058 --> 00:10:02.977
I, Hwang Seok-ho, will prepare thoroughly and be there.

00:10:07.524 --> 00:10:08.775
Right.

00:10:10.193 --> 00:10:12.612
Hwang Seok-ho, let's get that promotion!

00:10:14.155 --> 00:10:15.740
MAINTAIN ORDER IN THE SERVING LINE

00:10:21.704 --> 00:10:23.665
Why are you doing all that to a yellow croaker?

00:10:23.748 --> 00:10:25.625
You can just coat it in oil and fry it.

00:10:25.708 --> 00:10:27.877
Isn't that how you made the dish

00:10:27.961 --> 00:10:29.129
That we couldn't tell if it was a croaker or a goby?

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.382
What is this?

00:10:33.842 --> 00:10:36.344
Just eat it. Next.

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:38.555
Private First Class Tak Mun-ik!

00:10:53.987 --> 00:10:56.948
FRIED YELLOW CROAKER

00:11:14.716 --> 00:11:15.967
If I do this...

00:11:19.012 --> 00:11:22.015
It will be the perfectly fried yellow croaker.

00:11:30.565 --> 00:11:34.485
WELL-COOKED FRIED YELLOW CROAKER

00:11:34.569 --> 00:11:36.654
BUT NOT 5-STAR

00:11:37.739 --> 00:11:39.115
Well...

00:11:40.116 --> 00:11:41.534
This isn't it.

00:11:41.826 --> 00:11:44.037
Why? It looks delicious. I'll try it.

00:11:45.288 --> 00:11:48.833
WELL-COOKED FRIED YELLOW CROAKER BUT NOT 5-STAR

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:58.051
This sauce is insane! It's delicious.

00:11:58.134 --> 00:12:00.011
What am I missing? My gosh.

00:12:03.097 --> 00:12:05.558
I'm not just saying that. It's really delicious.

00:12:05.642 --> 00:12:07.393
So what are you so unhappy about?

00:12:07.602 --> 00:12:09.729
I don't know what the problem is.

00:12:09.812 --> 00:12:12.649
I mean, I need to know what the problem is

00:12:12.732 --> 00:12:15.693
So that I, Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun can decide whether or not to help you.

00:12:15.777 --> 00:12:17.862
There's this thing...

00:12:26.704 --> 00:12:29.415
- Geez. - Hey. What's with the sigh?

00:12:29.874 --> 00:12:33.002
So, I guess someone like me is no help to you now, right?

00:12:33.086 --> 00:12:34.254
You sucked up all my know-how

00:12:34.337 --> 00:12:35.922
During my final year of service, and now you don't need me?

00:12:36.005 --> 00:12:37.382
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

00:12:37.465 --> 00:12:41.803
If the food I make is, say, four stars

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:46.766
I feel like it's missing that one thing to make it five.

00:12:47.767 --> 00:12:49.560
But I just don't know what that is.

00:12:51.896 --> 00:12:53.773
Now you're talking like some kind of food critic?

00:12:53.856 --> 00:12:56.776
Hey, four stars, five stars... That's just you being greedy.

00:12:56.859 --> 00:12:59.654
It's not like we have a bunch of foodies around here.

00:12:59.737 --> 00:13:02.282
That kind of perfect food? That's for

00:13:02.615 --> 00:13:05.994
Somewhere like the Officers' Mess. They're not going to eat just anything.

00:13:07.912 --> 00:13:11.082
- You mean the Officers' Mess? - Yes, the Officers' Mess.

00:13:11.165 --> 00:13:13.126
The Battalion Commander specifically requested that I bring

00:13:13.209 --> 00:13:15.003
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae to the Officers' Mess.

00:13:15.086 --> 00:13:18.548
The Officers' Mess is already full of soldiers who are great cooks

00:13:18.631 --> 00:13:21.759
So why does he specifically want to eat Seong-jae's food?

00:13:22.635 --> 00:13:25.763
Come on, how can a person live on nothing but fine dining?

00:13:25.847 --> 00:13:27.473
I'm sure the Battalion Commander wants

00:13:27.557 --> 00:13:29.350
To hit up a snack bar every once in a while, too.

00:13:29.434 --> 00:13:31.144
This is to celebrate the Battalion Commander's promotion.

00:13:31.227 --> 00:13:34.314
And as a Company Commander, shouldn't I at least grant him this one request?

00:13:34.397 --> 00:13:37.400
I'm just not sure it's appropriate for me to attend such an important event.

00:13:37.483 --> 00:13:41.070
He specifically told me to bring you along, Ye-rin.

00:13:41.154 --> 00:13:42.822
Our Battalion Commander...

00:13:42.905 --> 00:13:46.617
He can be a bit scary when he's serious but he's a truly warm-hearted person.

00:13:50.246 --> 00:13:51.622
My goodness.

00:13:53.791 --> 00:13:56.919
Is our Private First Class Kang Seong-jae already wondering

00:13:57.003 --> 00:13:58.254
What dishes he should make?

00:13:58.421 --> 00:14:02.133
- Well, it's just... - Now, hold on.

00:14:02.216 --> 00:14:05.011
We can't actually serve the Battalion Commander snack food.

00:14:05.595 --> 00:14:08.806
It should be something a little luxurious, something.

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:11.559
A menu that makes him feel like he's being treated to something special.

00:14:12.143 --> 00:14:13.353
How should I put it? Something like...

00:14:13.436 --> 00:14:15.396
Like Korean royal cuisine.

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:17.523
Korean royal cuisine, all of a sudden?

00:14:17.815 --> 00:14:20.068
Why? How about sinseollo?

00:14:20.818 --> 00:14:23.571
Sinseollo, sir?

00:14:23.654 --> 00:14:26.449
Oh, does that have perilla powder in it too?

00:14:26.532 --> 00:14:29.202
Company Commander, don't you think overdoing it like that

00:14:29.285 --> 00:14:31.037
Will just make things worse?

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:33.289
Okay. Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

00:14:33.414 --> 00:14:35.083
Make sure to come up with a good idea.

00:14:35.792 --> 00:14:36.834
Got it?

00:14:41.005 --> 00:14:44.175
GANGLIM OUTPOST

00:14:44.258 --> 00:14:45.968
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae, are you ready?

00:14:46.177 --> 00:14:50.390
- You mean right now, sir? - Yes, come on, let's hurry.

00:14:50.473 --> 00:14:52.892
The Battalion Commander is waiting. Now, let's get it!

00:14:57.605 --> 00:14:58.731
ROSE-KNIFE

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:00.942
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun, I'm heading out.

00:15:01.025 --> 00:15:02.026
Salute!

00:15:02.235 --> 00:15:03.277
Yes, Salute.

00:15:09.867 --> 00:15:12.703
Then who's going to make lunch and do the dishes?

00:15:12.995 --> 00:15:15.498
My gosh. Don't go!

00:15:18.876 --> 00:15:20.002
Oh, right.

00:15:20.628 --> 00:15:21.629
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

00:15:21.712 --> 00:15:23.005
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae, sir.

00:15:23.089 --> 00:15:27.301
Are you ready to serve a perfect meal to everyone in here?

00:15:27.385 --> 00:15:30.179
Since you believe in me I'll do my absolute best.

00:15:30.263 --> 00:15:33.558
Let's show them Ganglim is a force to be reckoned with.

00:15:37.979 --> 00:15:39.772
HOGUK HALL

00:15:39.856 --> 00:15:40.898
Hero.

00:15:41.858 --> 00:15:43.776
A new map has been unlocked.

00:15:45.611 --> 00:15:47.029
STAGE: OFFICERS' MESS

00:15:47.113 --> 00:15:48.197
The Officers' Mess.

00:15:49.073 --> 00:15:51.826
Welcome to the Officers' Mess.

00:15:52.994 --> 00:15:55.037
STRONG WILL, WE ARE ONE! 29TH DIVISION, 1ST BATTALION

00:15:56.831 --> 00:16:00.084
- Congratulations on your promotion. - Congratulations!

00:16:02.378 --> 00:16:03.880
Salute!

00:16:03.963 --> 00:16:06.048
Captain Hwang Seok-ho, 4th Company Commander.

00:16:06.132 --> 00:16:08.301
Seok-ho, Ye-rin, you're here.

00:16:08.384 --> 00:16:11.846
If the Battalion Commander calls for me I'll be there, no matter where, sir.

00:16:11.929 --> 00:16:13.931
My sincerest congratulations on your promotion.

00:16:14.015 --> 00:16:15.475
This is all thanks to you for following my lead

00:16:15.558 --> 00:16:17.268
And helping me out, isn't it?

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:20.646
Oh, the Regimental Commander said he was curious

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:22.064
So I brought Private First Class Kang Seong-jae with me.

00:16:22.148 --> 00:16:23.149
Good.

00:16:23.232 --> 00:16:24.692
I hear the soldiers at Ganglim Outpost

00:16:24.775 --> 00:16:26.277
Have been gaining a lot of weight because of him.

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:28.237
That braised boneless pollock you made

00:16:28.321 --> 00:16:30.364
Had a completely unexpected flavor.

00:16:30.448 --> 00:16:32.074
- Nice. - Thank you.

00:16:32.158 --> 00:16:33.534
I knew you'd be like this.

00:16:33.868 --> 00:16:35.661
So, for the distinguished guests here

00:16:35.745 --> 00:16:36.913
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae

00:16:36.996 --> 00:16:38.664
Will showcase his cooking.

00:16:40.041 --> 00:16:43.211
- Oh, really? - Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

00:16:43.294 --> 00:16:45.296
It's an honor to be invited to such a special occasion.

00:16:45.379 --> 00:16:47.256
On the contrary, having you congratulate me

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:49.300
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae, I'm so flattered.

00:16:53.387 --> 00:16:54.931
GOURMET RATING

00:16:56.057 --> 00:16:57.642
GOURMET RATING

00:17:00.228 --> 00:17:03.773
GOURMET RATING

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:12.031
Five stars.

00:17:12.114 --> 00:17:14.909
Complete a five-star dish for the Regimental Commander.

00:17:14.992 --> 00:17:16.160
Why?

00:17:16.244 --> 00:17:19.247
- Sir? - Is there a fly on my head?

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:20.623
No, that's not it, sir.

00:17:20.706 --> 00:17:22.375
It's just that I sense the powerful aura

00:17:22.458 --> 00:17:24.377
Of a true gourmet from you, Regimental Commander.

00:17:26.128 --> 00:17:29.382
Gosh, this kid is a great judge of character.

00:17:29.465 --> 00:17:31.884
The Regimental Commander is very particular about his food.

00:17:31.968 --> 00:17:36.264
I mean, he even keeps a whole list of great restaurants on his phone.

00:17:36.347 --> 00:17:39.725
My wife is always nagging me to eat whatever

00:17:39.809 --> 00:17:42.103
But if you're going to eat something, it might as well be delicious, right?

00:17:42.186 --> 00:17:43.646
- Right. - That's right.

00:17:43.729 --> 00:17:46.440
A man doing such important work should only eat the best, shouldn't he?

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:50.278
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae, let's show him a delicious dish

00:17:50.361 --> 00:17:53.155
That's perfect for the Regimental Commander's

00:17:53.239 --> 00:17:54.365
Refined and noble palate.

00:17:55.533 --> 00:17:57.159
Yes, I'll get right on it.

00:17:57.243 --> 00:18:00.621
Hey, someone show this man to the kitchen.

00:18:00.705 --> 00:18:02.164
Yes, sir. I'll show him the way.

00:18:17.972 --> 00:18:20.641
- We don't have time. Let's move. - Yes, sir.

00:18:20.725 --> 00:18:21.726
How can I help you?

00:18:21.809 --> 00:18:23.352
Salute! Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

00:18:23.436 --> 00:18:24.687
I'm here to assist in the kitchen.

00:18:25.062 --> 00:18:28.190
Oh, you don't have to salute. We're informal here.

00:18:28.608 --> 00:18:29.734
Oh, okay.

00:18:29.817 --> 00:18:32.945
I was told to make a dish to celebrate the promotion.

00:18:33.029 --> 00:18:35.615
But what should I do? We weren't told anything about this.

00:18:36.532 --> 00:18:39.493
Let me check on that. Follow me.

00:18:45.291 --> 00:18:46.542
Corporal Lee Ho-yeong.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:49.837
This guy says he's from Ganglim Outpost

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:52.632
And that the Battalion Commander ordered him to cook.

00:19:01.182 --> 00:19:04.435
We have more than enough people here. Why bring in someone from Ganglim?

00:19:04.518 --> 00:19:05.561
That's what I'm saying.

00:19:06.687 --> 00:19:09.065
GOURMET RATING

00:19:10.816 --> 00:19:13.235
Gourmet Rating cannot be verified.

00:19:16.322 --> 00:19:18.115
Why are you staring at me like that?

00:19:18.199 --> 00:19:21.744
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae, 4th Company, Ganglim Outpost.

00:19:21.827 --> 00:19:22.870
I look forward to working with you.

00:19:22.953 --> 00:19:26.749
Outpost? I don't think a cook from an outpost can do anything here.

00:19:27.166 --> 00:19:29.251
We already have a full course menu planned

00:19:29.335 --> 00:19:31.128
So I don't think we can just give you something to do all of a sudden.

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:35.716
Well, then... I'll make a dish that I'm capable of.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:37.468
And if you do? When are you planning to serve it?

00:19:38.177 --> 00:19:41.055
- Pardon? - The dining sequence is part of the meal

00:19:41.138 --> 00:19:43.224
And we can't have your dish interrupting the flow.

00:19:45.309 --> 00:19:46.477
But still

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:48.270
If I make it delicious, shouldn't that be enough?

00:19:48.354 --> 00:19:50.147
Oh, is that right?

00:19:50.815 --> 00:19:52.316
You can cook over there.

00:19:52.441 --> 00:19:55.319
As for ingredients, open the fridge and grab whatever you need.

00:19:55.403 --> 00:19:56.487
Yes, I understand.

00:20:01.409 --> 00:20:02.952
Hey, who brought that guy in?

00:20:03.035 --> 00:20:04.495
They say he's from Ganglim Outpost.

00:20:05.454 --> 00:20:07.707
Gosh, he looks like a total dud.

00:20:07.873 --> 00:20:10.459
- This is going to be a pain. - Is the prep done?

00:20:10.543 --> 00:20:12.795
- Not yet, sir. - Then shut your traps and finish it.

00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:14.255
- Do we have enough time? - No, sir.

00:20:14.338 --> 00:20:16.382
If you're done chaming the perilla leaves, get the gastrique ready.

00:20:16.465 --> 00:20:19.885
- Yes, sir. - Chaming? Prep...

00:20:20.553 --> 00:20:22.388
What's a gastrique?

00:20:23.848 --> 00:20:28.436
Prep, gastrique. New keywords have been registered.

00:20:34.734 --> 00:20:36.652
I have to pull off a five-star dish

00:20:36.736 --> 00:20:38.320
That I've never even attempted before.

00:20:39.405 --> 00:20:42.825
First, I need to see what I can make with the ingredients they have.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:46.620
- Oh, I'm sorry. - Darn it.

00:20:53.252 --> 00:20:54.295
My goodness.

00:21:17.777 --> 00:21:18.778
GRADE A ORGANIC CARROTS FROM JEJU ISLAND

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:20.863
Grade A organic carrots.

00:21:21.155 --> 00:21:22.823
Grown healthily in Jeju's volcanic soil

00:21:22.907 --> 00:21:24.825
Without pesticides or chemical fertilizers.

00:21:25.117 --> 00:21:28.078
Gosh, even the carrots they get here are organic.

00:21:33.334 --> 00:21:36.754
Grade A Namhae spinach. Grown in the clean sea breeze

00:21:36.837 --> 00:21:38.464
Giving it thick leaves and a rich aroma.

00:21:38.547 --> 00:21:39.548
My goodness.

00:21:40.966 --> 00:21:43.010
Grade A Jeju black pork loin.

00:21:43.093 --> 00:21:46.305
Evenly marbled with fat, making it tender, not tough.

00:21:50.184 --> 00:21:51.685
With ingredients like these...

00:21:55.147 --> 00:21:56.190
Okay.

00:22:09.245 --> 00:22:12.164
I can tell how fresh it is just by the sound.

00:22:49.743 --> 00:22:50.744
Yes!

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:52.913
Okay, I've got it.

00:22:55.833 --> 00:22:58.168
It's come back to this. Braised boneless pollack.

00:22:58.794 --> 00:23:00.963
And without Kang Seong-jae, this is a huge problem.

00:23:01.505 --> 00:23:02.965
Hey, there.

00:23:03.215 --> 00:23:05.509
What are you doing all alone in your final year of service?

00:23:05.593 --> 00:23:07.678
Jeez, can't you tell?

00:23:07.761 --> 00:23:09.638
This is my punishment for getting a bad junior.

00:23:09.847 --> 00:23:12.224
Gosh, that Kang Seong-jae is really making things difficult for everyone.

00:23:12.308 --> 00:23:13.475
Look who's talking.

00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:16.687
- What are you doing in the kitchen? - What do you think?

00:23:16.979 --> 00:23:18.647
The company administration officer said not to leave you alone

00:23:18.731 --> 00:23:19.773
So he sent me to help out.

00:23:19.857 --> 00:23:22.651
No, I mean, there are plenty of other guys, so why you?

00:23:22.735 --> 00:23:23.986
Well...

00:23:24.069 --> 00:23:27.156
Who else can put up with Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun?

00:23:27.448 --> 00:23:29.575
They've just stuck the top two most senior guys

00:23:29.658 --> 00:23:32.786
At the outpost in the mess hall. What a total mess.

00:23:33.829 --> 00:23:36.832
So, what should I start prepping?

00:23:38.375 --> 00:23:39.460
It's...

00:23:42.630 --> 00:23:43.839
Braised boneless pollack.

00:23:46.175 --> 00:23:47.176
What?

00:23:50.304 --> 00:23:52.222
Braised boneless pollack without Kang Seong-jae?

00:23:54.266 --> 00:23:55.351
How are we supposed to make it?

00:23:59.563 --> 00:24:03.359
You have no idea how cute my daughter is.

00:24:04.401 --> 00:24:05.653
They say parents are a mirror for their children

00:24:05.736 --> 00:24:08.364
And she copies everything I do.

00:24:11.825 --> 00:24:14.870
I've taken her out for so much good food

00:24:14.954 --> 00:24:17.331
That she's become quite the picky eater.

00:24:18.916 --> 00:24:21.293
My son just sits around playing games all day.

00:24:21.377 --> 00:24:22.795
I have no idea who he takes after.

00:24:23.170 --> 00:24:25.297
It drives me crazy watching him. Absolutely crazy.

00:24:25.381 --> 00:24:28.842
But nowadays, gaming is considered a valuable skill, isn't it?

00:24:29.176 --> 00:24:30.970
The Republic of Korea is a powerhouse in e-sports

00:24:31.053 --> 00:24:33.347
So you never know he could become a great gamer.

00:24:33.430 --> 00:24:36.892
That's only if he's good at it.

00:24:37.184 --> 00:24:40.187
I don't know much about games, but from what I've seen

00:24:40.270 --> 00:24:42.189
He's really terrible at it.

00:24:42.731 --> 00:24:45.567
If you don't have the talent for something you should know when to quit.

00:24:45.651 --> 00:24:47.152
But he's stubborn about the wrong things.

00:24:50.280 --> 00:24:52.533
So, Outpost Commander, what were you like as a kid?

00:24:53.325 --> 00:24:54.451
Well...

00:24:55.035 --> 00:24:58.580
I think I was just an ordinary student.

00:24:59.081 --> 00:25:01.583
You know, quiet and unremarkable.

00:25:02.668 --> 00:25:05.045
That's surprising. I figured our Outpost Commander

00:25:05.129 --> 00:25:07.006
Would've been quite something back in school.

00:25:09.091 --> 00:25:10.509
The Company Commander would know, right?

00:25:10.592 --> 00:25:11.885
How stubborn our Outpost Commander is.

00:25:12.344 --> 00:25:13.554
Stubborn...

00:25:15.514 --> 00:25:17.766
She is, rather. Our Outpost Commander.

00:25:17.975 --> 00:25:20.644
Stubbornness. It's important.

00:25:21.562 --> 00:25:23.480
But telling the difference between determination

00:25:23.564 --> 00:25:26.483
And just being pigheaded, I think that's important too.

00:25:27.109 --> 00:25:29.737
Our people at Ganglim are all good.

00:25:30.029 --> 00:25:33.282
But I'm starting to see these little shortcomings one by one.

00:25:33.365 --> 00:25:34.825
I'm only saying this because it's a shame to see.

00:25:37.411 --> 00:25:38.454
Let's have a drink.

00:25:45.294 --> 00:25:46.503
Salute!

00:25:46.587 --> 00:25:49.757
This guy has a bit of main character syndrome.

00:25:50.507 --> 00:25:51.967
I was a little late carrying out

00:25:52.051 --> 00:25:54.219
A grave mission befitting my new rank.

00:25:54.303 --> 00:25:55.596
And you got the job done?

00:25:55.679 --> 00:25:57.014
Yes, of course.

00:26:00.309 --> 00:26:01.393
Nice.

00:26:02.061 --> 00:26:04.354
I've been working all day and haven't had a single decent meal.

00:26:05.147 --> 00:26:06.482
Thanks, 4th Company Commander.

00:26:07.775 --> 00:26:10.235
But you must not be very busy over there

00:26:10.611 --> 00:26:11.695
Seeing as you got here so early.

00:26:41.600 --> 00:26:43.393
If you stir-fry it for too long

00:26:43.477 --> 00:26:45.562
The texture of the noodles will be ruined.

00:26:46.146 --> 00:26:49.316
The noodles might get soggy, so be careful.

00:27:16.969 --> 00:27:19.054
Just mix the ingredients and it's ready to go out.

00:27:19.138 --> 00:27:20.222
Just the ingredients.

00:27:29.731 --> 00:27:30.858
My goodness.

00:27:30.941 --> 00:27:32.734
When the Regimental Commander dined with us before

00:27:32.818 --> 00:27:35.737
I heard him mention he eats lotus root for his circulation

00:27:36.071 --> 00:27:37.781
So I prepared some fried lotus root chips.

00:27:37.865 --> 00:27:41.702
I fried thinly sliced lotus root, and topped it with beef tartare.

00:27:41.785 --> 00:27:45.164
- Please enjoy. Salute! - Thanks.

00:27:45.581 --> 00:27:48.292
I guess you have to be this good to be a soldier in the Officers' Mess.

00:27:48.375 --> 00:27:51.336
This is why I can't help but adore this guy.

00:27:51.795 --> 00:27:53.380
All right, then. At a time like this

00:27:53.463 --> 00:27:55.174
Shouldn't we launch one of our missiles?

00:27:55.257 --> 00:27:58.135
Regimental Commander, your timing is perfect as always.

00:28:02.014 --> 00:28:04.308
All right, missile.

00:28:04.391 --> 00:28:08.395
- For the future, for love, for work! - Launch!

00:28:22.409 --> 00:28:24.995
The terrifying braised boneless pollack.

00:28:25.621 --> 00:28:27.915
Don't you think we should at least do something?

00:28:28.582 --> 00:28:30.334
You saw what Kang Seong-jae was doing, didn't you?

00:28:30.417 --> 00:28:32.544
I saw it. I only watched, though.

00:28:32.628 --> 00:28:34.129
Who knew a day like this would come again?

00:28:34.213 --> 00:28:35.464
And that I'd have to do it alone?

00:28:35.964 --> 00:28:39.134
Hey, that hurts. Really. You're not alone.

00:28:39.218 --> 00:28:40.469
While you were on leave

00:28:40.552 --> 00:28:42.262
I worked hard to get back to my old prime.

00:28:42.346 --> 00:28:43.388
So then...

00:28:43.889 --> 00:28:45.724
- Just the two of us? - Yes.

00:28:45.807 --> 00:28:47.184
Shouldn't we show these kids

00:28:47.267 --> 00:28:48.936
We didn't eat all that army food for nothing?

00:28:51.480 --> 00:28:54.191
Right. We may not be as good as Kang Seong-jae

00:28:54.274 --> 00:28:55.400
But we can do this.

00:28:55.484 --> 00:28:56.985
- Yes! - Let's do this!

00:29:07.829 --> 00:29:09.539
What? Wait a minute.

00:29:09.623 --> 00:29:10.874
- Why? - What's wrong?

00:29:13.293 --> 00:29:14.461
What is going on here?

00:29:14.628 --> 00:29:16.630
Hey, where did Kang Seong-jae go? And why is that guy here?

00:29:16.713 --> 00:29:19.591
What? Kang Seong-jae was called to the Officers' Mess.

00:29:19.675 --> 00:29:23.262
- Darn it. This is driving me nuts. - Hey, what's on the menu today?

00:29:26.390 --> 00:29:30.477
- Why? - It's braised boneless pollack.

00:29:32.020 --> 00:29:35.232
I tasted it for seasoning, and it's not bad, okay?

00:29:35.315 --> 00:29:36.775
So just take one bite

00:29:36.858 --> 00:29:40.779
And give me your honest, truthful opinion.

00:29:41.154 --> 00:29:42.531
The fact that Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun tasted it

00:29:42.614 --> 00:29:43.991
Is what's really scary.

00:29:45.450 --> 00:29:48.036
Hey! I can't take it. Let's go.

00:29:52.291 --> 00:29:54.584
Where do you think you're going?

00:29:55.168 --> 00:29:57.087
This is the masterpiece of Ganglim's top two cooks.

00:29:57.170 --> 00:29:58.630
Don't complain and go eat.

00:29:58.797 --> 00:30:01.425
I'll tell the company administration officer that you're skipping your meal.

00:30:01.508 --> 00:30:02.884
Oh, dear.

00:30:02.968 --> 00:30:05.095
Do you really think this makes any sense?

00:30:05.178 --> 00:30:07.014
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

00:30:10.767 --> 00:30:11.768
Get in here.

00:30:22.362 --> 00:30:24.239
The last beef bone soup was edible

00:30:24.406 --> 00:30:25.741
So maybe the pollack will be good too?

00:30:25.824 --> 00:30:26.992
Corporal Joo Sang-uk.

00:30:27.075 --> 00:30:29.411
Do you know why people fall for scams?

00:30:29.911 --> 00:30:33.081
At first, they're really nice to you. They make you trust them.

00:30:33.165 --> 00:30:35.167
Then the moment your suspicion fades

00:30:35.250 --> 00:30:37.336
They take everything you have in one fell swoop.

00:30:38.754 --> 00:30:40.380
So you're saying the beef bone soup was bait?

00:30:40.464 --> 00:30:41.590
Of course.

00:30:42.132 --> 00:30:44.634
Didn't I say I could do it too?

00:30:44.718 --> 00:30:46.553
The moment you think, "Looks okay,"

00:30:46.636 --> 00:30:48.722
And take a bite it's over.

00:30:48.805 --> 00:30:50.849
No one stick your spoons in there carelessly.

00:30:50.932 --> 00:30:51.975
You'll be a goner.

00:30:56.521 --> 00:30:59.232
- Eat. - Darn it.

00:31:00.692 --> 00:31:01.902
Whatever.

00:31:07.741 --> 00:31:10.035
What? Oh!

00:31:11.161 --> 00:31:13.413
I feel like they were really going for it with this one.

00:31:13.497 --> 00:31:15.290
Hey, I'm telling you, you're being scammed.

00:31:21.213 --> 00:31:22.214
What?

00:31:22.297 --> 00:31:23.757
What's going on right before he's discharged?

00:31:28.762 --> 00:31:29.763
What?

00:31:30.764 --> 00:31:33.266
Isn't it a bad sign when a person changes all of a sudden?

00:31:33.350 --> 00:31:34.476
This is delicious.

00:31:37.396 --> 00:31:38.522
It's delicious!

00:31:44.611 --> 00:31:46.571
- Darn it. - Hey! Get it away!

00:31:46.655 --> 00:31:48.281
We really don't get along.

00:31:51.326 --> 00:31:55.956
KANG SEONG-JAE'S RECIPE NOTE

00:32:41.168 --> 00:32:45.172
JAPCHAE

00:32:45.255 --> 00:32:47.424
Japchae. Four stars.

00:32:47.591 --> 00:32:49.468
I followed the recipe perfectly.

00:32:49.551 --> 00:32:51.011
Let's get ready to serve the main dish!

00:32:51.094 --> 00:32:52.220
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

00:32:53.138 --> 00:32:54.681
If it's not a five-star dish

00:32:54.764 --> 00:32:56.766
It won't satisfy Regimental Commander.

00:32:57.434 --> 00:33:00.061
How can I get that final star?

00:33:00.937 --> 00:33:04.524
At this rate, the quest will be a complete failure.

00:33:11.907 --> 00:33:13.033
Hey.

00:33:13.241 --> 00:33:16.536
- Are you taking that out now? - Yes. I'm about to.

00:33:17.037 --> 00:33:18.371
- Let's take this out too. - Yes.

00:33:18.455 --> 00:33:19.831
Wait, hold on a second.

00:33:19.956 --> 00:33:21.958
Why? Is there something else you need to do?

00:33:23.627 --> 00:33:24.669
Well...

00:33:25.545 --> 00:33:28.673
It's just it feels like it's missing a little something.

00:33:30.800 --> 00:33:31.885
Let me taste it.

00:33:44.940 --> 00:33:46.316
It seems fine.

00:33:51.112 --> 00:33:52.280
Should we serve it like this?

00:33:58.537 --> 00:34:01.373
No. It's not good enough yet.

00:34:18.181 --> 00:34:19.599
The dish we've prepared for you today

00:34:19.683 --> 00:34:22.894
Is duck leg, marinated for 24 hours in salt and various herbs.

00:34:22.978 --> 00:34:24.312
It was slow-cooked for three and a half hours

00:34:24.396 --> 00:34:26.106
In 65°C duck fat to create this duck confit

00:34:26.189 --> 00:34:28.858
Which we've paired with an orange gastrique sauce.

00:34:28.942 --> 00:34:30.610
Please enjoy the texture of the crispy duck skin

00:34:30.694 --> 00:34:33.572
Along with the tender meat.

00:34:33.655 --> 00:34:36.700
Gosh, is this really the same duck dish we're used to?

00:34:37.993 --> 00:34:38.994
On such a special day

00:34:39.077 --> 00:34:42.038
We felt an ordinary dish wouldn't properly convey our congratulations

00:34:42.122 --> 00:34:43.540
So we put a great deal of care into it.

00:34:43.623 --> 00:34:44.666
Please, enjoy your meal.

00:34:45.125 --> 00:34:46.167
Thanks!

00:34:50.630 --> 00:34:55.218
Gosh, just the smell of this makes me feel full already.

00:34:56.386 --> 00:34:58.096
Please eat, Regimental Commander.

00:34:59.055 --> 00:35:01.683
- Oh, yes. Let's dig in. - Yes, sir.

00:35:10.066 --> 00:35:11.818
JAPCHAE: SQUEEZE WATER FROM SPINACH, ADD SALT AND SESAME OIL AND TOSS

00:35:11.901 --> 00:35:13.486
SOAK GLASS NOODLES IN WATER, CUT THE ONION INTO BITE-SIZED PIECES

00:35:17.490 --> 00:35:18.617
Darn it.

00:35:19.117 --> 00:35:22.621
I feel like I need to find the solution before I can start over.

00:35:22.829 --> 00:35:24.789
- Let's serve dessert. - Yes.

00:35:34.841 --> 00:35:37.093
This feels more like a wake than a feast.

00:35:42.098 --> 00:35:44.559
- May I ask you something? - Yes, what is it?

00:35:44.768 --> 00:35:47.395
When you make a dish that isn't satisfactory

00:35:47.854 --> 00:35:49.856
How do you find a way forward?

00:35:50.607 --> 00:35:53.693
Until I can serve a dish that makes them pick up their utensils again

00:35:54.277 --> 00:35:55.528
I'd just keep cooking.

00:35:55.695 --> 00:35:56.696
On and on.

00:35:57.614 --> 00:36:00.116
This dish is how they're going to remember you, right?

00:36:19.844 --> 00:36:22.639
- Darn it, what is he doing? - Just leave him be.

00:36:23.181 --> 00:36:26.142
- Let's see what he's got. - Yes, understood.

00:36:36.444 --> 00:36:38.947
Japchae. Four stars.

00:36:45.537 --> 00:36:49.165
Add a special ingredient to upgrade the dish's class.

00:37:21.489 --> 00:37:23.491
WILD PINE MUSHROOMS, GRADE S FROM ULJIN, GYEONGBUK

00:37:23.575 --> 00:37:26.995
Wild pine mushrooms. Grade S.

00:37:30.248 --> 00:37:33.334
So Grade S ingredients really do exist.

00:37:34.127 --> 00:37:35.128
Its aroma is so intense

00:37:35.211 --> 00:37:38.256
It fills your mouth with flavor even without any special preparation.

00:37:44.012 --> 00:37:46.264
Who would take a knife to wild pine mushrooms?

00:37:47.015 --> 00:37:48.850
You have to tear it along the grain to keep the aroma intact.

00:37:50.185 --> 00:37:51.269
Oh, I see.

00:37:53.229 --> 00:37:54.773
I didn't know that. Thank you.

00:38:16.711 --> 00:38:21.132
WILD PINE MUSHROOM JAPCHAE

00:38:21.216 --> 00:38:23.176
Wild pine mushroom japchae.

00:38:23.635 --> 00:38:27.680
By adding a Grade S ingredient, one star is added.

00:38:27.764 --> 00:38:29.808
GUILTY OF BEING TOO DELICIOUS

00:38:30.099 --> 00:38:33.019
All right. Thanks to Corporal Lee Ho-yeong

00:38:33.478 --> 00:38:38.358
From the appetizer to the dessert, we've enjoyed a full-course meal.

00:38:39.067 --> 00:38:40.485
We should have promotions more often.

00:38:40.568 --> 00:38:42.654
So we can eat lavish dishes like this.

00:38:43.822 --> 00:38:45.406
If I had my way

00:38:45.490 --> 00:38:48.576
I almost wish Corporal Lee Ho-yeong's discharge date would never come.

00:38:48.952 --> 00:38:51.120
If you were to eat delicious food like this on the outside

00:38:51.204 --> 00:38:53.665
- how much would you have to pay? - That's right.

00:38:55.500 --> 00:38:56.584
What?

00:38:58.586 --> 00:39:01.589
- I'm sorry I'm late. - Come to think of it

00:39:01.673 --> 00:39:04.467
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae's dish is finally being served.

00:39:04.759 --> 00:39:07.387
Isn't this japchae?

00:39:07.470 --> 00:39:10.265
Yes. It's japchae made with wild pine mushrooms.

00:39:11.099 --> 00:39:12.350
Can't you see

00:39:12.433 --> 00:39:14.018
That we've already finished our meal, dessert and all?

00:39:14.102 --> 00:39:17.272
No, let's at least hear his reason for making it.

00:39:18.022 --> 00:39:21.234
Of all the possible dishes, why did you choose japchae?

00:39:23.862 --> 00:39:25.029
I chose it because

00:39:25.113 --> 00:39:27.115
It's an essential dish for a feast like this one.

00:39:27.949 --> 00:39:31.703
Well, you're not wrong, but since it's japchae

00:39:32.412 --> 00:39:34.205
I have to admit I'm not really looking forward to it.

00:39:34.289 --> 00:39:37.375
We should have discussed the menu. I'm sorry, sir.

00:39:44.090 --> 00:39:48.720
Gosh, but the aroma of the pine mushrooms is quite wonderful.

00:40:05.695 --> 00:40:06.821
Order in the court.

00:40:06.905 --> 00:40:09.574
Your Honor, the defendant armed itself with its aroma

00:40:09.657 --> 00:40:11.534
And bewitched the people.

00:40:13.036 --> 00:40:14.245
Objection.

00:40:14.412 --> 00:40:18.207
The defendant couldn't help its own inherent aroma.

00:40:18.291 --> 00:40:20.710
Overruled. Continue, prosecutor.

00:40:23.046 --> 00:40:25.506
Furthermore, by simultaneously expressing

00:40:25.590 --> 00:40:28.343
Both chewy and crunchy textures, it has gotten people addicted

00:40:28.426 --> 00:40:30.053
And made it impossible for them to stop.

00:40:30.136 --> 00:40:31.304
Leading the witness.

00:40:31.387 --> 00:40:34.015
The people ate it of their own free will.

00:40:34.098 --> 00:40:37.727
Your Honor, on the charge of utterly captivating people's minds

00:40:38.937 --> 00:40:41.230
I indict the defendant, pine mushroom japchae.

00:40:42.690 --> 00:40:45.443
THE DEFENDANT

00:40:50.073 --> 00:40:53.034
THE JUDGE

00:40:53.117 --> 00:40:54.285
I will now pass sentence.

00:40:54.494 --> 00:40:55.787
The defendant, japchae.

00:40:56.871 --> 00:40:58.873
The defendant, japchae, is guilty.

00:41:01.125 --> 00:41:03.544
Guilty of being too delicious.

00:41:07.298 --> 00:41:09.092
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae is guilty!

00:41:10.843 --> 00:41:14.514
- What? - Oh, no.

00:41:14.764 --> 00:41:16.516
This is absolutely excellent.

00:41:18.685 --> 00:41:20.561
So the good morale in the 4th Company lately

00:41:20.645 --> 00:41:23.106
- was all thanks to the food. - That's right.

00:41:23.189 --> 00:41:25.441
Gosh, your skills have improved quite a bit

00:41:25.525 --> 00:41:26.901
Since that braised boneless pollack.

00:41:26.985 --> 00:41:29.362
Thank you, sir. Maybe because this is the Officers' Mess

00:41:29.445 --> 00:41:31.322
It was possible because of the great ingredients

00:41:31.406 --> 00:41:32.907
Like the pine mushrooms.

00:41:32.991 --> 00:41:34.742
Precious pine mushrooms?

00:41:34.826 --> 00:41:35.994
Of course

00:41:36.077 --> 00:41:38.830
The aroma of the pine mushrooms played a big part in the japchae

00:41:38.913 --> 00:41:40.623
But the spinach, onions, and carrots

00:41:40.707 --> 00:41:43.001
Were of much better quality in the Officers' Mess.

00:41:45.962 --> 00:41:48.172
Are you saying ingredients to the Officers' Mess

00:41:48.256 --> 00:41:50.341
And the Mess Hall are different?

00:41:51.968 --> 00:41:53.720
Support Section Chief, what is going on here?

00:41:53.803 --> 00:41:55.013
Well...

00:41:55.555 --> 00:41:58.182
It seems there was some kind of mistake.

00:41:58.933 --> 00:42:01.519
As far as I know, of all the provisions that come into the Mess Hall

00:42:01.602 --> 00:42:02.979
There haven't been any problems with any of them.

00:42:03.062 --> 00:42:04.897
The difference in the food ingredients

00:42:05.898 --> 00:42:07.108
Is a fact.

00:42:09.068 --> 00:42:10.236
Outpost Commander.

00:42:10.987 --> 00:42:12.780
Are you sure you know what you're talking about?

00:42:13.114 --> 00:42:15.491
Since we just signed a provisions contract with a new company

00:42:15.575 --> 00:42:16.784
It's possible that

00:42:16.868 --> 00:42:19.412
The previous supplier intentionally delivered poor-quality provisions.

00:42:19.495 --> 00:42:21.622
But I was never informed of anything.

00:42:21.831 --> 00:42:23.916
Actually, this isn't something that just started happening...

00:42:25.001 --> 00:42:26.169
I'm sorry.

00:42:26.252 --> 00:42:29.255
We should investigate this further and then report back.

00:42:29.338 --> 00:42:30.423
I apologize.

00:42:33.342 --> 00:42:35.511
Let's not mess around when it comes to food.

00:42:35.887 --> 00:42:37.180
Battalion Commander, investigate this thoroughly

00:42:37.263 --> 00:42:41.059
- and report back to me. Understood? - Yes, sir.

00:43:00.787 --> 00:43:01.871
Hero.

00:43:02.246 --> 00:43:05.750
You have completed the Five-Star Quest.

00:43:06.709 --> 00:43:10.588
As a reward, you have acquired dessert and other cooking recipes.

00:43:20.556 --> 00:43:21.557
Thank you.

00:43:21.641 --> 00:43:23.810
Thanks to you, I was able to finish the dish I wanted to make.

00:43:25.812 --> 00:43:27.897
It doesn't seem like you've formally studied cooking.

00:43:29.232 --> 00:43:31.109
I first started cooking after I joined the army.

00:43:31.776 --> 00:43:36.155
Anyone could tell. You looked a bit clumsy and awkward.

00:43:37.782 --> 00:43:40.076
I thought I'd improved a lot since I started

00:43:40.785 --> 00:43:42.495
But after coming to the Officers' Mess

00:43:42.578 --> 00:43:44.956
I truly feel like I was a frog in a well.

00:43:45.331 --> 00:43:48.417
There are so many amazing cooks here.

00:43:50.128 --> 00:43:52.380
I didn't expect you to suddenly serve japchae.

00:43:53.005 --> 00:43:55.883
In a way, I guess you could call it bold.

00:43:56.467 --> 00:43:58.427
- Thank you. - That wasn't a compliment.

00:43:59.220 --> 00:44:02.306
Even so, I've really learned a lot today.

00:44:05.768 --> 00:44:07.603
Could you bring me some of the japchae you made earlier?

00:44:13.860 --> 00:44:16.154
Doesn't he usually avoid eating food made by others?

00:44:16.320 --> 00:44:19.323
He does. He hates ruining his palate.

00:44:32.336 --> 00:44:33.504
What do you think?

00:44:49.604 --> 00:44:51.272
You seemed so unsure of yourself, so I was worried.

00:44:53.191 --> 00:44:54.317
But it's better than I expected.

00:44:57.278 --> 00:44:58.362
Thank you.

00:44:59.572 --> 00:45:00.740
Well, but...

00:45:01.282 --> 00:45:03.534
If it's not too much to ask

00:45:03.743 --> 00:45:07.705
May I also try the dish you made?

00:45:16.464 --> 00:45:18.507
- Try it. - Thank you.

00:45:19.258 --> 00:45:23.012
I don't think I've ever had a dish that looks like this.

00:45:25.473 --> 00:45:27.475
It's a French dish called duck confit.

00:46:12.478 --> 00:46:14.272
France, the land of gourmet food.

00:46:17.316 --> 00:46:18.734
The moment I take a bite

00:46:18.818 --> 00:46:23.572
I feel like I'm in the place that every chef dreams of.

00:46:25.783 --> 00:46:26.993
My mouth is filled.

00:46:27.410 --> 00:46:31.414
"This is French cuisine!" It feels like it's shouting that.

00:46:44.010 --> 00:46:47.805
Duck confit, six stars.

00:46:47.888 --> 00:46:50.433
DUCK CONFIT IT'S ENTRANCING AND BEAUTIFUL...

00:47:04.530 --> 00:47:07.742
It's so delicious. It's absolutely divine.

00:47:16.917 --> 00:47:18.669
Why are you being so nice to that guy?

00:47:18.753 --> 00:47:20.588
Don't you guys learn anything from watching him?

00:47:20.671 --> 00:47:22.631
We can make japchae with our eyes closed.

00:47:22.715 --> 00:47:25.885
You guys, who cook complacently, thinking "This is good enough"?

00:47:43.110 --> 00:47:44.195
I'm sorry.

00:47:44.612 --> 00:47:46.572
The Outpost Commander brought up something she didn't have to.

00:47:47.198 --> 00:47:48.240
Seok-ho.

00:47:50.326 --> 00:47:53.412
- Yes, Battalion Commander. - It's not confirmed yet

00:47:54.038 --> 00:47:56.374
But when I get promoted and transferred to headquarters

00:47:56.457 --> 00:47:58.250
I'm thinking of having you by my side.

00:48:02.129 --> 00:48:03.381
Are you serious, sir?

00:48:03.464 --> 00:48:06.634
It's more important for me to work with people I can trust.

00:48:08.386 --> 00:48:09.470
I see.

00:48:10.679 --> 00:48:14.683
I had no idea you thought so highly of me, Battalion Commander.

00:48:14.767 --> 00:48:16.560
Well, you always seem so disappointed.

00:48:16.936 --> 00:48:19.855
Anyway, I'm planning on taking you with me, all right?

00:48:21.357 --> 00:48:25.403
Yes, sir. I understand completely.

00:48:25.861 --> 00:48:26.862
Good.

00:48:37.248 --> 00:48:39.041
You should start looking out for yourself now, shouldn't you?

00:48:39.875 --> 00:48:43.129
From now on, I'll take good care of you so you won't feel left out.

00:48:43.212 --> 00:48:44.255
Don't worry.

00:48:46.799 --> 00:48:49.260
70TH ANNIVERSARY OF THE ARMY FOUNDING

00:48:51.846 --> 00:48:53.264
IM SEUNG-BIN

00:49:09.989 --> 00:49:13.033
I thought I had received a skill that was too good for me

00:49:14.368 --> 00:49:17.455
But there are so many people far more talented than me.

00:49:18.664 --> 00:49:20.332
And I've become curious about the path ahead of me

00:49:20.416 --> 00:49:23.335
And just how endlessly it stretches on.

00:49:24.837 --> 00:49:26.046
How can I...

00:49:26.881 --> 00:49:29.091
Learn even more?

00:49:33.304 --> 00:49:34.388
I apologize.

00:49:36.515 --> 00:49:39.185
You shouldn't have done something you'd need to apologize for.

00:49:39.518 --> 00:49:40.561
Right?

00:49:41.479 --> 00:49:42.480
Yes, sir.

00:49:43.939 --> 00:49:46.442
They told you to do a thorough comprehensive inspection

00:49:47.526 --> 00:49:50.446
- so do it right. - I will handle it properly.

00:49:51.030 --> 00:49:52.031
Min-gu.

00:49:53.532 --> 00:49:55.701
You get what I'm saying, right?

00:49:58.913 --> 00:49:59.997
Yes.

00:50:01.415 --> 00:50:02.666
Starting with Ganglim Outpost

00:50:03.667 --> 00:50:04.752
I will proceed.

00:50:04.960 --> 00:50:06.962
BATTALION COMMANDER'S OFFICE

00:50:18.974 --> 00:50:22.561
60TH REGIMENT, 1ST BATTALION GANGLIM

00:50:22.686 --> 00:50:23.687
Before roll call next Tuesday

00:50:23.771 --> 00:50:25.648
You are scheduled to watch an educational program

00:50:25.731 --> 00:50:26.857
On soldiers' human rights.

00:50:27.566 --> 00:50:30.444
- Sir, Company Commander. - What is it? We're in a meeting.

00:50:32.196 --> 00:50:33.197
Well...

00:50:34.198 --> 00:50:36.325
I think you need to go to the mess hall right now.

00:50:37.785 --> 00:50:38.827
Here you go.

00:50:38.911 --> 00:50:40.996
- Let's hurry up and get some rest. - Yes, sir.

00:50:44.917 --> 00:50:46.752
All right, freeze!

00:50:46.877 --> 00:50:48.170
INSPECTION

00:50:48.879 --> 00:50:50.339
What? Salute!

00:50:50.881 --> 00:50:52.424
As of this moment

00:50:52.508 --> 00:50:55.594
I'm conducting a comprehensive inspection of Ganglim Outpost.

00:50:57.638 --> 00:51:00.140
Nice to see you. Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

00:51:01.183 --> 00:51:02.268
We keep running into each other, don't we?

00:51:38.971 --> 00:51:41.432
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

00:51:41.890 --> 00:51:43.392
We will now conduct an inspection of all personnel

00:51:43.475 --> 00:51:45.185
At Ganglim Outpost.

00:51:45.477 --> 00:51:47.146
You are here to be investigated.

00:51:47.229 --> 00:51:49.148
Then stop trying to railroad us

00:51:49.231 --> 00:51:50.733
And please conduct a proper investigation.

00:51:50.816 --> 00:51:54.695
What if I go and ask the Regimental Commander myself?

00:51:54.778 --> 00:51:55.904
Are you confident?

00:51:56.155 --> 00:51:58.407
Hey, this has to be the church the Regimental Commander

00:51:58.490 --> 00:52:01.452
- comes to every Sunday, right? - I made this to give to your daughter.

00:52:01.994 --> 00:52:03.495
Are you here, So-yul?

00:52:03.954 --> 00:52:05.539
If we give up now, the Outpost Commander will...

00:52:05.623 --> 00:52:07.541
How can you do this so suddenly?

00:52:07.750 --> 00:52:10.210
I'm thinking this might be a good chance to clean up Ganglim.

